   "value": "## Findings (200 digits, $\\theta=(1/3,-8/57)$; one chain point, two twist directions)\n\n**The zero-twist formula carries over to [3,1,0] ⊗ [2,1,0]. Only the measure and $c$ change, as suspected.**\n\n- **Measure (section 4).** $M=\\Gamma_h[\\nu_1]/\\Gamma_h[\\nu_3^{[2]}]$ with per-site weights, i.e. poles $\\theta_1+\\{0,1,2,3\\}$, $\\theta_2+\\{0,1,2\\}$ (7 poles).\n  - Twisted identity at $\\varepsilon=10^{-3}$: orthogonality $2\\times10^{-131}$ (12 states of weight (2,2,3)); one $C_{\\rm vac}$ for all 120 states to $6\\times10^{-160}$.\n  - $1/(\\nu_1\\nu_2\\nu_3)$ fails orthogonality ($6\\times10^{34}$). The full ladder $\\{0,1,2,3\\}$ at both sites is orthogonal but the normalization fails (spread 507).\n- **Constant $c$ (section 5), derived.** The twisted $w$-identity with $\\Delta T_2=\\prod_s(u-\\theta_s-\\lambda^{(s)}_1-1)(a_1u+b_1)+\\prod_s(u-\\theta_s-\\lambda^{(s)}_3)(a_2u+b_2)$ holds on 360 rows (0 at 167 digits). At zero twist $b_1+b_2-\\Delta c_1=7a_1$ on all 42 pairs, so $c=6=\\#\\text{poles}-1$ (5 and 7 for the equal-site cases).\n- **Boxed formula (section 6).** With $c=6$ and $E_\\lambda$ **unchanged**, $\\mathcal B_A/\\mathcal B_{\\rm vac}$ matches the physical limit to $10^{-19}$–$10^{-22}$ for all 7 highest-weight states. $c=5$ or $7$ misses by 1–34%.\n  - Physical limits: 42 → 1, 24 → 10.36915, 15′ → 10.31429, 15₁ → 92.76173, 15₂ → 181.92272, $\\bar6$ → −531.34549, 3 → 1867.31533.\n- **Evidence level.** Measure and $c$: independently validated (the twisted identity and the zero-twist relation, then the separate boxed-limit test). $E_\\lambda$: the equal-site formula, not refitted, reproduces the required ratios 8, 5/4, 90, 90, 180, 720. It is still not derived. Only one chain point was used.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 7. Column operations on calN (exact algebra): det calN = -det calN'' with, for G_ij = q^j(u) q_i(u-1),\n   calN'' = ( <D+ G>, <c q^j q_i - u D+ G>, <q^j D- q_i> ),  D+f = f(u+1) - f(u), D-f = f(u) - f(u-1).\n   Check against the original columns for all 7 states, and at a wrong c for contrast. ---- *)\nClearAll[NmOldX, NmNewX, colTabX];\nNmOldX[m_, c_] := Module[{s = untwNX[[m]], q, qd},\n   q = Function[{i, x}, qpolyX[s[\"q\"][[i]], x]]; qd = Function[{j, x}, qpolyX[s[\"qd\"][[j]], x]];\n   Table[{\n     bracketX[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x] - qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n     bracketX[Function[x, x qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - (x - c) qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n     bracketX[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]]}, {ij, tripleX}]];\nNmNewX[m_, c_] := Module[{s = untwNX[[m]], q, qd, G},\n   q = Function[{i, x}, qpolyX[s[\"q\"][[i]], x]]; qd = Function[{j, x}, qpolyX[s[\"qd\"][[j]], x]];\n   G = Function[{i, j, x}, qd[j, x] q[i, x - 1]];\n   Table[With[{i = ij[[1]], j = ij[[2]]}, {\n      bracketX[Function[x, G[i, j, x + 1] - G[i, j, x]]],\n      bracketX[Function[x, c qd[j, x] q[i, x] - x (G[i, j, x + 1] - G[i, j, x])]],\n      bracketX[Function[x, qd[j, x] (q[i, x] - q[i, x - 1])]]}], {ij, tripleX}]];\ncolTabX = Table[{nameX[[m]], N[Abs[-Det[NmNewX[m, cHX]]/Det[NmOldX[m, cHX]] - 1], 3],\n    N[Abs[-Det[NmNewX[m, cHX + 1]]/Det[NmOldX[m, cHX]] - 1], 3]}, {m, 7}];\nGrid[Prepend[colTabX, {\"multiplet\", \"|-det calN''/det calN - 1|\", \"same with c+1 in calN'' (contrast)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
